From: Gentoo
Subject: [PATCH] Update bundled CMake setup for CMake 4

CMake 4 removed compatibility with CMake versions older than 3.5, so the
historic 2.x declarations now prevent configuration.  Use 3.10 for both
bundled projects after testing their configuration and the complete LMMS
build with CMake 4.

The native VST bridge is explicitly a C++-only project.  Do not pass it a
CMAKE_C_FLAGS definition: the same NATIVE_LINUX_VST definition is already
passed through CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS, while the C-only variable can never affect
any target and causes CMake's unused-command-line-variable warning.

--- a/src/3rdparty/ringbuffer/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/3rdparty/ringbuffer/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 2.8)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)
 
 # settings
 project(ringbuffer)
--- a/plugins/FreeBoy/game-music-emu/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/plugins/FreeBoy/game-music-emu/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -12 +12 @@
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 2.6 FATAL_ERROR)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)
--- a/plugins/VstBase/NativeLinuxRemoteVstPlugin64.cmake
+++ b/plugins/VstBase/NativeLinuxRemoteVstPlugin64.cmake
@@ -10 +9,0 @@
-			"-DCMAKE_C_FLAGS=-DNATIVE_LINUX_VST"
